# Finder "open with" defaults per file type. Applied by set-default-apps.swift
# from install.sh; drift.sh runs the same tool with --check.
# Format: <bundle id>  <.extension or UTI>
#
# macOS asks "Do you want all documents with the extension … to open with …?"
# for every type that actually changes — no supported API avoids that. The tool
# skips types already pointing at the right app, so re-runs are silent, and it
# applies changes one at a time so you get one dialog at a time, not a stack.
#
# Only types the target app declares in its Info.plist can be assigned to it.
# That is why e.g. .env, .tf, .jsonc and .pem are absent — VS Code does not
# declare them, and LaunchServices refuses the assignment.
#
# Left alone on purpose: images/PDF → Preview, .psd → GIMP, .svg/.html →
# browser, .csv/.xlsx → Numbers, .docx → Pages, .zip/.tar → Archive Utility.

